@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP systems. Split shared nine-owner artifact into core and separate ProjectForge artifacts; keep future systems deferred.
title MVP implementation artifacts — distinct system releases
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam wrapWidth 190
package "Resumefolio core — proposed internal modules" {
 component "Identity / invited admission\nPresentation / Sharing\nApplications / Files and Operations" as C
 artifact "IA-01 core application artifact\nCore UI / migrations / operating templates" as A
 C --> A : core-only composition
}
package "ProjectForge — separate system" {
 component "Repository / transport authority\nFile-history / issues / simple Kanban" as G
 artifact "ProjectForge artifact and database\nNative Git Smart HTTP / Laravel\nSeparate MySQL 8.4 / same host, separate OS user" as P
 G --> P : separately owned realization
}
A <--> P : authenticated user-scoped API\nno shared database / transaction assumed
rectangle "Native Git client\nCommits normally created here" as CL
CL --> G : authorized clone / fetch / pull / push
rectangle "AFTER MVP\nPrivate communications system via API\nAdvanced Git / Sprint / YAML execution" as F #F8EBD7
legend bottom
 Logical owners are retained; nine owners are not forced into one application release.
 Core private uploads/media remain on the Resumefolio server.
 This is artifact responsibility, not a selected ProjectForge engine or deployment.
endlegend
@enduml
